WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:26.860
While heading to Alcatraz for the finals, a kid named Noa trapped us in a virtual world.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.740
I want to pummel Marik and save Mai.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.540
But unless I win my duel, I can't escape.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.760
And he'll take over my body.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.610
I'm dueling one of The Big Five - Judge Man.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.010
But his objections are taking me off my game.

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:49.020
Gamble For Victory

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.520
It's your turn.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:55.530
Yeah, I know.  I draw.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.730
Kamionwizard has 1300 attack points.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:07.510
I can destroy it if I use my Deck Master's entire ability on Swordsman of Landstar.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.220
But I'm worried about that set card.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.850
What if it's a trap card?

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.000
I have no choice.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.160
Panther Warrior has more attack points, so I'll use it to defend and see what happens.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.490
I summon Panther Warrior!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.620
And I set a card!

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:37.500
Kamionwizard has 1300 attack points, so it can't destroy Panther Warrior.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.510
Even if he raises its attack points, I'll use Skull Dice to power it down.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.250
This isn't my favorite plan, but it's all I can do for now.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.250
I end my turn.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.180
My turn.  I draw.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.350
I flip over my set card.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:03:00.640
The Continuous Trap Leading Question activates.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:07.970
When a Level 4-or-below Fusion Monster battles your monster...

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:11.070
...Leading Question raises its attack points by 800.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:14.070
Kamionwizard attacks!

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.880
H-Hold on!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.160
I knew you'd power it up!

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.640
I'm making my move!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.410
Skull Dice!

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.020
All right!

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.760
What?  One?

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.500
Since I rolled a 1, your monster's attack points don't go down!

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:47.300
I told you that I can change black into white.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.680
Since my Fusion Monster Kamionwizard dealt you damage...

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.970
...my Continuous Spell Sinister Justice activates.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:05.110
I gain 800 life points.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.490
Damn!

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.500
A duel is unpredictable until the end.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.080
Jonouchi!

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.450
C'mon!  He turned the tables on you!

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.150
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.000
Be quiet!

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.010
Jonouchi, it's your turn.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:30.050
When a Fusion Monster battles, Leading Question gives it 800 attack points.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:37.760
So I need a monster with at least 2100 attack points to destroy Kamionwizard.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:45.630
But I only have Swordsman of Landstar, and it has 500 attack points.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.080
What's wrong?

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:52.270
Since you used your Deck Master's ability early, you're paying for it now.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.010
Whatever!

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.740
Damn.  I hope I draw a good card.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.240
Hurry up and draw.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.250
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.250
Graceful Dice.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:09.110
I'll use this to power up Swordsman of Landstar's attack points.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.080
I summon Swordsman of Landstar!

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:19.150
And I'll use Graceful Dice to power it up!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.470
Go!

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.340
Yeah!  Success!

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:37.310
1 again?  No way!

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.910
Two 1's in a row.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.110
Jonouchi is unlucky.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:42.800
Yeah.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.090
I activate my Deck Master's ability.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.420
Life Sentence!

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:57.730
This is bad.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.600
I have no monsters.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.070
What should I do?

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.020
Jonouchi...

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:11.050
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:14.050
My turn.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.830
Pot of Greed.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.050
Pot of Greed?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:25.800
Since you no longer have any cards in your hand, I bet you really want this card.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:33.500
Due to Pot of Greed's effect, I draw two cards from my deck.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.510
You now have six cards in your hand.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:41.500
The trap card Gamble!

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:51.020
When you have at least six cards in your hand and I have less than two, I can activate this card.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:52.580
Gamble?

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:53.520
Yeah.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.320
Jonouchi guesses heads or tails.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:01.030
If he's right, he draws until he has five cards in his hand.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.400
Jonouchi has no cards in his hand right now.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:10.410
But if he guesses wrong, his next turn is skipped.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:12.910
C'mon.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:19.420
If Lady Luck is on my side, then bring me luck this time!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.320
This is perfect.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.840
Thinking "I'll be lucky this time" over and over leads to self-destruction.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.260
That's why gambling is scary.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.280
I flip my coin!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.020
The ocean?

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:51.450
Noa has put a lot of work into this.

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:57.150
Dammit!  I thought we finally escaped from the virtual world!

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:00.270
Noa really ticks me off!

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.340
I bet he has no friends!

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.250
Keep telling him off.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:10.000
Because I know he's watching us.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.000
Are you listening, Noa?

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:19.940
You'll pay dearly for mocking us with your lame virtual images!

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.600
Prepare for the worst!

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:28.690
Seto, it's fun to see you annoyed.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.690
Anyway, how's the duel going?

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:42.730
Heads!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.240
Tails?  I lost again.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.800
He's wrong again?

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:53.240
Jonouchi.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.730
The outcome will always be the same.

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:00.750
I only take cases that I can win.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.370
Damn!

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:05.250
I activate the Quick-Play Spell Scapegoat!

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.260
It's pathetic that you're still fighting.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:16.000
My turn isn't over yet.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.500
I activate the spell Reinforcement of the Army!

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.040
I add a Level 4-or-below Warrior-Type monster in my deck to my hand.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.820
Then I shuffle my deck.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:30.680
I activate the spell card Polymerization from my hand.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:34.750
I fuse Armaill and One-Eyed Shield Dragon from my hand.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.910
I summon Dragoness the Wicked Knight!

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.510
Another Fusion Monster with low attack points?

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:50.030
My trap won't activate unless it has at least 1500 attack points.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:56.550
And Leading Question only raises their attack points when he attacks.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.700
Damn!  I'm in trouble!

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.010
Kamionwizard attacks Scapegoat!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:14.880
Dragoness the Wicked Knight also attacks Scapegoat!

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.500
I end my turn.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.300
Damn!  It's my turn!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:32.170
Since Gamble failed, you skip your turn.

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:34.180
Oh yeah...

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.410
My turn.  I draw.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:40.160
Kamionwizard attacks Scapegoat.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:47.620
Dragoness the Wicked Knight attacks Scapegoat.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:54.130
They're all gone.

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.200
I end my turn.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.440
Zero cards in your hand, zero monsters on your field.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:03.140
Katsuya Jonouchi, here's your verdict.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.510
You lose this duel.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:13.300
I rolled a 1 for both Skull Dice and Graceful Dice.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:14.320
Damn!

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.530
Gamble also failed.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.780
How unlucky can I be?

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.820
Pull yourself together, Jonouchi!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.460
You still have your turn!

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:27.540
Don't give up!

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:32.830
But luck has totally forsaken me.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.340
It's pointless to continue.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:36.970
Jonouchi...

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:42.340
Isn't it weird that he missed three times in a row?

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:43.880
Yeah.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:46.850
I was thinking the same thing.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.200
Failing three times in a row.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:53.360
It may be coincidence, but...

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.860
Something's up.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.860
Is this a set up?

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.860
This duel is canceled.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.720
Noa!

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.770
Noa?

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.720
That boy is...

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.230
Noa?

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.970
This duel is canceled.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:43.970
Why?

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.970
What?  Why, Noa?

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:51.210
I'm about to defeat Katsuya Jonouchi!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:56.220
Did you think I wouldn't notice your cheating?

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.220
What?  Cheating?

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.550
Yes, Jonouchi.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:08.230
Ooka cheated so that all your gambling cards would fail.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.140
What?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.970
Is that true?

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.560
I thought so.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:18.470
But isn't Noa on his side?

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:21.980
Noa, this is part of my plan.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:27.980
It's not like we're competing in the Olympics.

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.080
So a little-

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.520
Don't oppose me.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:38.490
If you win by cheating, you haven't actually defeated Seto Kaiba's allies.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:43.230
So I won't have truly surpassed Seto Kaiba.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.730
Truly surpass me?

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.740
Why is he so obsessed on being my rival?

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.080
Is someone else behind this?

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.110
Someone pitting us against each other?

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.900
Only one man would do that.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:06.260
Gozaburo Kaiba.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.060
But that's impossible.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:10.100
He's dead.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:16.110
Who is Noa?

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.050
I now understand.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:23.270
All my gamble cards failed because you cheated.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:28.510
That means luck hasn't forsaken me.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.510
Jonouchi, the duel is canceled.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:36.520
Ooka, you will be held responsible for this.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.020
B-But...

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:39.750
Let us play.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.090
What?

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.090
Cheating's fine.

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.590
There's always cheating in gambling.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.830
But a duel is a serious fight!

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:56.840
Once a duel begins, nothing can stop it before it's over!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.200
Jonouchi!

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.580
Are you serious?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.000
Oh?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:05.310
You're nothing more than an extra to me.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.520
So if you want to lose, then go ahead.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.170
He gave his OK.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:14.050
Are you in, Mr. Lawyer?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.540
I'll tell you one thing.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:21.790
Once I take a case, I never abandon it.

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.600
Then it's decided.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.340
You were depressed a moment ago...

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:30.400
...but your attitude changed when you learned I was cheating.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.040
You're so naive!

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:39.200
Even if you know that I cheated, can you actually improve your situation?

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:42.710
I won't know unless I try.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:46.920
Because luck hasn't forsaken me yet!

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.420
What a fool.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.420
Here I go!  My turn!

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:51.420
I draw!

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.690
Look!  I also drew it!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.200
I activate the spell card Pot of Greed.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.200
Nice!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.300
I draw two cards.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:06.400
My drawing power is still excellent!

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.180
I summon my Deck Master, Flame Swordsman!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:16.170
I equip him with the Equip Spell, Burning Soul Sword!

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:21.520
Burning Soul?

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:26.050
But Burning Soul requires a tribute!

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.020
Yeah.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:30.300
Simply equipping Burning Soul is pointless.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:37.380
By tributing my monster, its attack points are added to the equipped monster for one turn.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.770
It's a cursed sword that slays its allies.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:44.900
But you have no monsters to tribute.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.380
And your Deck Master only has 1000 attack points.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:54.970
How will you defeat my Fusion Monster that has over 2000 attack points?

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.080
How funny!

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.460
Wait, Mister.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.980
I still have one card left.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:10.400
The spell card Arduous Decision!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.310
Arduous Decision.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:16.680
You draw two cards from your deck, and your opponent chooses one of them.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:17.780
What do you mean?

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:24.280
If the opponent picks a monster card, it'll be summoned to the field.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:28.790
But if it's not a monster card, it's sent to the graveyard.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.000
I believe in my luck!

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:38.730
Choose one.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.820
I'll tell you this.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:45.300
One is the monster card Goblin Attack Force.

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:49.680
The other is the spell card Shield & Sword.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.450
You're telling me your cards?

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:57.620
If you choose the spell card, you win.

00:17:57.620 --> 00:18:00.920
But if you choose Goblin Attack Force...

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:06.930
...I'll tribute it to Burning Soul, and Flame Swordsman will have 3300 attack points.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:09.170
T-That means...

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:14.080
If you attack Dragoness the Wicked Knight that has 2000 attack points...

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:17.900
...I'll lose 1300 life points, dropping me to 0!

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:20.910
That's why you're a lawyer.  You're good at math.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:23.680
So?  Right or left?

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:24.940
Pick one.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.420
Nice plan, Jonouchi!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:30.680
This way, he can't cheat!

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:33.250
It's a real gamble: 50/50!

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:37.990
Only a fool would think of this strategy.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.460
But it's still one in two.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.500
He has a 50% chance of losing.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:48.100
Anzu, we have to believe in Jonouchi's luck.

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:51.610
Come on.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.470
It's one in two.

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:55.110
Choose one.

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:02.920
The card on your left.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.450
Are you sure?

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.920
Are you absolutely sure?

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.980
Nice try.

00:19:11.980 --> 00:19:14.610
You almost fooled me.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:18.570
You only had to confirm once.

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:22.120
But by confirming twice, you gave yourself away!

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:28.800
I've overcome countless battles!

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:31.410
You can never outwit me!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.950
Your left card is a spell card.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:36.520
I'm absolutely sure.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:42.420
Katsuya Jonouchi, you lose this du-

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.130
Actually, I choose the right card!

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:49.130
So this one?

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:52.000
Too bad.

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:54.470
All right!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:58.860
Due to Arduous Decision's effect, I summon Goblin Attack Force!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:08.080
I tribute Goblin Attack Force to activate Burning Soul Sword's effect!

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:21.260
Here I go!

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:25.930
My Deck Master Flame Swordsman attacks Dragoness the Wicked Knight!

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:29.200
Prepare yourself!  Burning Soul!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.110
But I...

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:42.610
I've deceived so many fools so far...

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:48.980
But I was tricked by this kid?

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:54.860
Oh yeah!  I won this duel!

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.080
You did it, Jonouchi!

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.240
Jonouchi!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.500
I did it!

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:04.650
Huh?  Where did Noa go?

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:08.180
He probably left to prepare for the next duel.

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:11.610
Next duel?  Who's dueling next?

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:14.460
Kaiba or Otogi...

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:18.120
Or maybe Shizuka!

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.280
What?

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.120
Jonouchi!

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.120
Don't be silly!

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:24.120
Shizuka doesn't know how to duel!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.730
Yeah.  That's why we have to find them quickly.

00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.130
Of course!

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:31.200
Damn!

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.420
Jonouchi!

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:33.640
Jonouchi!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.120
Just wait, Shizuka!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.740
I'm coming!

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:55.100
Since Jonouchi won, The Big Five are down to two.

00:21:55.100 --> 00:22:00.000
But won't they target Shizuka because she has no dueling experience?

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.360
I knew it!  Shizuka has started dueling!

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:06.160
What?  Otogi and Honda are with her?

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:09.300
Since it's 3-on-1, they appear to have the advantage.

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:12.860
But Honda is an amateur.  Will they be OK?

00:22:13.070 --> 00:22:16.530
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
A Man's Path  Honda's Honorable Defeat

00:22:16.530 --> 00:22:18.040
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:28.990
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:37.940
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:42.910
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:42.910 --> 00:22:46.880
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:47.310 --> 00:22:54.850
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:58.420
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:03.190
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:13.300
And walk it without stopping

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:20.910
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:29.880
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:37.860
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:47.700
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
